Template: dolphone/modem-access
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Let Dolphone send setup commands to the modem?
 Dolphone sets the modem up for calls (USB call audio, VoLTE, the carrier
 profile), sends where call audio goes each time the modem starts, and handles
 call forwarding and caller-ID codes, all as AT commands. ModemManager passes
 those on only in its debug mode, which this turns on.
 .
 Debug mode also makes ModemManager's log more detailed, and with this modem
 that log can include phone numbers and texts; and it lets any program running
 as you send the modem AT commands. On the Flipper One, call audio needs it.
 .
 You can change this later: sudo dolphone-modem-access on (or off), or
 sudo dpkg-reconfigure dolphone.
